Third-party components
----------------------

AuctionNet
  This repository does not package the full AuctionNet simulator, its original
  datasets, or its model checkpoints. A few compatibility helpers and native
  simulator parameters in env/auctionnet_sim_env.py are adapted from
  AuctionNet's run/run_test.py and Controller/Controller.py, including winner
  selection, over-cost handling, and default advertiser configurations.
  AuctionNet is licensed under Apache License 2.0. Users must obtain the full
  simulator separately from its official repository and comply with its license:

      https://github.com/alimama-tech/AuctionNet

  The default location expected by this code is:

      AuctionNet/

  and can be overridden with the ADCOEVO_AUCTIONNET environment variable.

  AuctionNet's simulated auction, PV generation, exposure and conversion sampling,
  and its native heterogeneous competitor strategies are used as an external
  dependency. The auction mechanics themselves are not reimplemented here.

Base language model
  LoRA adapters and evaluation require a base causal language model of the user's
  choice. Model weights are not distributed with this repository; users must obtain
  them and comply with their license terms. Configure the path with ADCOEVO_BASE_MODEL.

Datasets
  No SFT data, trajectory dumps, experiment results or checkpoints are included.
  The market profiles in configs/auctionnet_profiles.yaml are ready to use:
  Sparse records AuctionNet's native simulator settings, while General uses
  parameters calibrated from public General data. The preparation script can
  regenerate profile assets from archives the user provides.

Value metric
  ADV in this project is a proxy computed on top of AuctionNet auction outputs
  (predicted conversion value times the fixed business target CPA). It is not real
  advertiser revenue or GMV.
